<title>GERMANY: Bundesbank details M3 developments in February.</title>
<headline>Bundesbank details M3 developments in February.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bundesbank published the following data relating to M3 money supply in February. AGGREGATE (in bln marks)	  Feb96  Jan96  Feb95   End97</p>
<p>Level 1) BANK LENDING TO DOMESTIC</p>
<p>   NON-BANKS (total)	     +32.9  +11.7  +28.2   4826.6</p>
<p>   Lending by Bundesbank	  +0.0   +0.0   -0.0	8.7</p>
<p>   Lending by banks		+32.9  +11.7  +28.2   4817.9</p>
<p>    To firms and individuals   +23.3  - 6.0  +16.8   3641.1</p>
<p>of which</p>
<p>     short term lending	  + 4.5  -21.1   +2.6    601.7</p>
<p>    To public authorities	+ 9.6  +17.7  +11.4   1176.8</p>
<p>2) NET EXTERNAL ASSETS</p>
<p>OF CREDIT INSTITUTIONS</p>
<p>   AND THE BUNDESBANK	    -10.2  -48.8   -3.6    285.7</p>
<p>3) MONETARY CAPITAL FORMATION</p>
<p>   FROM DOMESTIC SOURCES, TOTAL+17.3  + 7.4  +12.7   2781.4</p>
<p>of which</p>
<p>Time deposits</p>
<p>     4 yrs and more		 +5.0   +4.9  +10.0   806.6</p>
<p>Savings deposits over 3 mths</p>
<p>   notice, savings certificates -1.5   -5.5   -3.4   498.0</p>
<p>Bank debt securities</p>
<p>     in circulation		+11.0   +5.9   +3.8  1137.2</p>
</text>
